# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 6 of the Tutorial (Part 1)

[Bo2's Example 4.15]

j,0,1,t
c,1,0,2,0

analysis: tr
note: In this problem, we run a transient (TR) analysis and describe a capacitor for the first time. The source's value is t itself; find the voltage across the capacitor, and then its value at t = 2 s, which is 1 V. The Solve card is how version 9 does the calculator's `|t=2`. Naming t as an unknown is what makes the second equation bite.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/bo2e0415.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes
solve_equations: x = vc
solve_equations: t = 2
solve_unknowns: x, t


[Bo2's Example 5.1 (DC, for the initial condition)]

e,1,0,V
r1,1,2,r1
c,2,0,c
r,2,0,r

analysis: dc
note: The DC half of a two-interval problem: for t < 0 the circuit has long settled, so a DC solve gives the capacitor's voltage — the initial condition the next entry needs.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-5-1-2.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 5.1 (TR)]

c,2,0,c,r*v/(r+r1)
r,2,0,r

analysis: tr
note: The TR half: the capacitor carries the initial condition found in DC, and vc decays as e^(-t/(c*r)) times r*v/(r+r1).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-example-5-1-2.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.1 (DC)]

j,0,1,2
r,1,0,3
c,1,0,1/12

analysis: dc
note: First interval, t < 0: solve in DC for the capacitor's voltage. It is 6 V — the initial condition vc0 of the next entry.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-1-3.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.1 (TR)]

j,0,1,0
r,1,0,3
c,1,0,1/12,vc0

analysis: tr
note: Second interval: the source at zero and vc0 as the initial condition. Find vc and ic: 6e^(-4t) and -2e^(-4t).
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-1-3.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


