[Bo2's Figure 5.10a]

l,1,0,l,il0
r,1,0,r

analysis: tr
note: In this problem, we describe an inductor (the l element) for the first time. Given iL(0) = il0, find vL(t), iL(t) and vR(t), symbolically.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-figure-5-10a-7.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Example 5.3 (DC)]

e,1,0,v
r1,1,2,r1
l,2,0,l
r2,2,0,r

analysis: dc
note: First interval of the RL problem, in DC: find il, the inductor's initial condition — v/r1.
