[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.3 (DC)]

e,1,0,8
r4,1,2,4
l,2,0,1
r12,2,0,12

analysis: dc
note: Find iL(t), vL(t) and i(t) for all t; this first interval in DC gives the initial condition, 2 A. The chapter asks for ir1 here; this circuit's resistors are r4 and r12, and the 2 A it prints is ir4.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/bo2s-drill-exercise-5-3-9.jpg
rounding: exact
si: no
units: yes


[Bo2's Drill Exercise 5.3 (TR)]

